Fix wrong buffer pointer passed to parseCapabilityCCCParams

parseCapabilityInfo() passes &capsInfoData[index] together with &index, but
parseCapabilityCCCParams() indexes the buffer with *index itself. The offset
is therefore applied twice and the CCC capability values are read from the
wrong position (possibly beyond the response buffer). Pass the base pointer.

--- a/libs/uwb-iot/uwb_api/Api/UwbApi_Internal.c	2026-11-10 14:02:05.353405786 +0800
+++ b/libs/uwb-iot/uwb_api/Api/UwbApi_Internal.c	2026-11-10 14:02:05.358405713 +0800
@@ -2839,7 +2839,7 @@
         if ((extParamId & EXTENDED_PARAM_ID_MASK) == CCC_INFO_ID) {
             length = capsInfoData[index++];
 #if UWBFTR_CCC
-            if (parseCapabilityCCCParams(pDevCap, extParamId, &index, length, &capsInfoData[index]) == FALSE) {
+            if (parseCapabilityCCCParams(pDevCap, extParamId, &index, length, capsInfoData) == FALSE) {
                 NXPLOG_UWBAPI_W("Error Parsing CCC Params.");
                 status = FALSE;
             }
